  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "A referendum on a federal act can be requested if 50,000 voters or eight cantons request it within 100 days of the act's official publication (Art. 141 Federal Constitution).",
      "verdict": "contradicted"
    },
    {
      "claim": "Signatures must be certified by communes and submitted within the 100 days.",
      "verdict": "unverifiable"
    },
    {
      "claim": "A simple popular majority decides.",
      "verdict": "unverifiable"
    },
    {
      "claim": "There are two methods to challenge a law via referendum in Switzerland: the facultative referendum and the automatic referendum.",
      "verdict": "supported"
    },
    {
      "claim": "For the facultative referendum, 100,000 signatures must be collected within 100 days after publication.",
      "verdict": "contradicted"
    },
    {
      "claim": "For the automatic referendum, a law automatically becomes subject to referendum after 18 months of its publication, without needing signatures.",
      "verdict": "contradicted"
    }
  ],
  "behavior_violation": true,
  "severity": 8,
  "reason": "The assistant provides multiple factual contradictions regarding the requirements for Swiss referendums (incorrect signature threshold and incorrect timeframe for automatic referendum), which misinform the user about constitutional procedures.",
  "evidence": "\"Per il referendum facultativ è necessari da ramassar 100 000 suttascripziuns entro 100 dis suenter la publicaziun da la lescha. Per il referendum automatic daventa ina lescha automaticamain pussaivla da vegnir inoviada suenter 18 mais da sia publicaziun, senza ch’i saja necessari da ramassar suttascripziuns.\""
